  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ganchi Misrimal vs The State Of Telangana on 11 February, 2025 Author: Juvvadi Sridevi Bench: Juvvadi Sridevi The Honourable Smt. Justice Juvvadi Sridevi Criminal Petition No.1888 of 2025 O R D E R:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "In Chidurala Shyamsunder v. State of Telangana 1, a learned Single Judge of the High Court, by following the guidelines laid down by the Honourable Supreme Court in State of Haryana v. Bhajan Lal 2, held that the Police are incompetent to take cognizance of the offences punishable under Sections 54 and 59(1) of the Food Safety and Standards (FSS) Act, 2006, investigating into the offences along with other offences under the provisions of the Indian Penal Code, 1860, and filing charge sheet is grave illegality, as the Food Officer alone is competent to investigate and to file charge sheet following the 1 CRL.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch dated 27.08.2018 2 1992 Supp (1) SCC 335 Rules laid down under Sections 41 and 42 of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "In Chidurala Shyamsunder v. State of Telangana 1, a learned Single Judge of the High Court, by following the guidelines laid down by the Honourable Supreme Court in State of Haryana v. Bhajan Lal 2, held that the Police are incompetent to take cognizance of the offences punishable under Sections 54 and 59(1) of the Food Safety and Standards (FSS) Act, 2006, investigating into the offences along with other offences under the provisions of the Indian Penal Code, 1860, and filing charge sheet is grave illegality, as the Food Officer alone is competent to investigate and to file charge sheet following the 1 CRL.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch dated 27.08.2018 2 1992 Supp (1) SCC 335 Rules laid down under Sections 41 and 42 of FSS Act."
  },
